60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: So, what are the actual options on the table? I need to see the full list before I can weigh the risks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: I’m listening. I need to see how each option handles the hesitation I found in the turnout data.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,- **Takumi**: I’m waiting. I need to see which option actually fixes the imbalance I found in the sign-in sheets.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,- **Toshio**: I am ready. I need to see which option minimizes the administrative burden I found in the logs.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: I’m ready. I need to see which option makes the first step small enough for the people on those taster forms.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Jonathan, I’m leaning toward the flat fee. It’s simple, and it stops the constant chasing that broke the last treasurer.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, I worry a flat fee feels like a trap to the hesitant members I found. It might deepen the hesitation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Mio, a flat fee ignores the eighteen ghosts. If they pay the same as the core nine, the resentment will explode.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: @Mio, the flat fee is the only one that keeps the treasurer’s hours near zero. The others multiply the chasing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, I worry a flat fee feels like a trap to the hesitant members I found. It might deepen the hesitation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Toshio, simplicity is vital, but @Kenji is right. If the flat fee scares off new members, we lose future income.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, I agree. The tiered option might work. It lets newcomers start small, easing that fear of a whole-year commitment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Jonathan, named grades caused friction before. I refuse to let the core nine carry the weight while others hide in a lower tier.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the minute books show the friction, but the logs show the labor. A tiered system still requires tracking who is in which tier.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, I’m worried the tiers will make the fee structure too visible. Newcomers need to drift in, not be sorted into boxes.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Jonathan, I hear you, but @Toshio’s warning about tracking tiers is real. If it’s too complex, we’re back to chasing money.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, I understand the tracking risk. But the activity-based option lets people pay only for what they use, removing the upfront fear.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Jonathan, activity-based charging is a disaster. It means chasing money at every single event. The treasurer will quit again.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, you are right. Activity-based charging means six hours of chasing per month. I cannot support that.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: @Takumi, you are right. Activity-based charging means six hours of chasing per month. I cannot support that.""}]}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, I hear you, but the taster forms show people fear the whole year. Activity-based charging feels like a series of small traps, not a safe drift in.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
